avid here that the stronger  her maturity the better it will be for  this country  now you've been very  loud and clear in this interview with  your praise for Teresa mayor you're  clearly a fan of the work she's doing do  you think she's doing a better job than  you would have done if you'd been  elected oh yes you do  why is that well I think that you know  the proof of the pudding is in the  eating  the the demonstration of the way in  which Teresa has made all the major  calls on brexit successfully the obvious  popularity that she enjoys the stability  and strength that she's brought to that  role  all of these reflect incredibly well on  her judgment and her leadership  abilities and so all I can do is take a  step back and admire the way in which  she has on the economy on education and  on Europe showing a degree of  consistency and clarity as leader  there's something else as well during my  leadership run brief as it was one of  the things that I tried to articulate  was the need for the Conservatives to do  more for people on average and below  average incomes and actually to be fair  Teresa she was on to this issue before  me and she's delivered on this issue far  more energetically I think than anyone  could have expected any conservative  leader could have done and the result of  that focus on ordinary working families  has been popularity in the polls but  also a conservative party bringing  forward proposals including on areas  like new council housing but reflect the  interests of the overwhelming majority  now you know any person in your  household unflinching in their support  of Teresa mayor your wife wrote a column  saves backing up her idea of boys and  girls jobs in the house so you do do  carry acne boys jobs quickly what's your  jobs in the house yes I do what I'm told  I'm in in in our home much as in the  country I'm very very happy that a  strong woman is in charge  very sensible answer there Michael Gove  thank you very much for coming on the  show thank you

